   "id": "s1_01",
   "speaker": "lobe",
   "text": "You own something right now that you have absolutely no use for."
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_02",
   "speaker": "lobe",
   "text": "Maybe it's a kitchen gadget that can turn a cucumber into seventeen different shapes. Maybe it's a shirt with the tag still on. Or maybe it's that mystery cable you've been keeping since 2017, just in case NASA calls.",
   "say": "Maybe it's a kitchen gadget that can turn a cucumber into seventeen different shapes. Maybe it's a shirt with the tag still on. Or maybe it's that mystery cable you've been keeping since twenty seventeen, just in case NASA calls."
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_03",
   "speaker": "lobe",
   "text": "And here's the strange part: when you bought it, it seemed like a fantastic idea."
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_04",
   "speaker": "lobe",
   "text": "So how can your brain be completely convinced you NEED something on Tuesday... and completely forget it exists by Friday?"
  },
  {
   "id": "s1_05",
   "speaker": "lobe",
   "text": "Today we're investigating one of humanity's most expensive hobbies: buying nonsense."
  }
